  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming Higher Education Systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  USAID&apos;s Transforming Higher Education Systems activity in Malawi will foster productive partnerships between U.S. and Malawi higher education institutions (HEIs) to address issues of educational access, equity, relevance, and quality. Transforming Higher Education Systems activity will prioritize strengthening Malawian universities&apos; capacities to increase market-linked program offerings, research and innovation in areas relevant to the country&apos;s economic growth with specific attention to agriculture and value addition. With FY 2022 funds, Transforming Higher Education Systems activity will work to: strengthen the human and institutional capacities of Malawian HEIs to design and deliver high quality, diversified, and market-relevant degrees and short courses; expand access to these high quality higher education courses, particularly for adolescent girls and young women, people with disabilities, students graduating from community day secondary schools especially in rural areas, and other disadvantaged youth; improve research and innovation outputs from Malawian HEIs; improve collaboration between Malawian HEIs and industry; improve governance systems of the Malawian higher education sub-sector, including governance of Malawian HEIs; and strengthen or establish student protection systems at Malawian HEIs.This activity will increase access to quality education and support the Integrated Country Strategy Goal 3: human capital development, specifically under Mission Objective 3.3 - Malawi expands educational opportunities to equip its citizens with foundational and marketable skills responsive to Malawi&apos;s public and private sector needs. It also furthers the goals of the USAID&apos;s 2020-2025 CDCS which seeks to support Malawi to become more self-reliant, gender equitable, and democratically accountable..</narrative>
  </description>
